meta {
  name: 02 - Update
  seq: 2
}

docs {
  Update paths for an existing document, created by `01 - Create`. Every request here
  targets `{{documentId}}` (set by "Direct Upload (PUT)" in `01 - Create`) - run that
  request first, or manually set `documentId`/`documentVersion` collection variables to an
  existing document's id/version.

  Two independent axes:
  - Metadata-only update vs. metadata + new file (the latter bumps back through the full
    ingestion workflow: `CREATED -> UPLOADED -> INDEXED` plus re-classification/summary).
  - Direct (`PUT`, file bytes in the request) vs. presigned (`POST`, returns a MinIO PUT
    URL for the client to upload to separately) - mirrors the same two shapes as create.

  `DocumentUpdateRequest` metadata **replaces** the existing metadata map; it does not
  merge with it.
}
